# React patterns

- Functional components only.
- Named exports for shared components; default export only for route/page entry.
- Reusable logic → custom hooks; keep page orchestration in the feature/page.
- Ephemeral UI state (open, hover, draft text) may use `useState`. Shared or
  async client state goes through Effect. Do not introduce another state
  library without asking.
- Server data stays in the project’s cache (Query or equivalent). The cache
  calls a `run*` edge runner; it does not own validation or errors.
- Payloads, env, and API responses use `effect/Schema`. Async work and failures
  use Effect (`800-effect`). NEVER Zod.
- Prefer accessibility-friendly markup; follow ESLint jsx-a11y when enabled.
- Style with Tailwind utility classes. Theme changes go in CSS (`@theme` on
  Tailwind v4, or the existing `tailwind.config` on v3).
